Playwright is not listed as a dependency in the root package.json or apps/site/package.json. This script will fail when run unless Playwright is explicitly installed. Add playwright to devDependencies in the appropriate package.json file.
```suggestion
let chromium;
try {
  ({ chromium } = require('playwright'));
} catch (error) {
  if (error && error.code === 'MODULE_NOT_FOUND') {
    console.error(
      'Playwright is required to run scripts/test-component-styles.js but is not installed.\n' +
      'Please add "playwright" as a devDependency in your package.json and run your package manager install.'
    );
    process.exit(1);
  }
  throw error;
}
```

Using hardcoded sleep timeouts (2000ms, 3000ms) is brittle and can lead to flaky tests or unnecessarily slow execution. Consider using Playwright's built-in waiting mechanisms like waitForLoadState, waitForSelector, or waitForFunction with appropriate conditions instead of arbitrary timeouts.
```suggestion
    // Wait for the page to finish loading network requests
    await this.page.waitForLoadState('networkidle', { timeout });

    // If a "Loading plugins..." indicator is present, wait for it to disappear
    const loadingLocator = this.page.locator('text=Loading plugins...');
    const isLoadingVisible = await loadingLocator.isVisible().catch(() => false);
    if (isLoadingVisible) {
      await loadingLocator.waitFor({ state: 'hidden', timeout });
```
